<p>
Virtua Grotesk is a neo-grotesque sans-serif built on a hidden mathematical
grid. Every curve and angle aligns to powers of two &mdash; a dyadic,
self-labeling coordinate system that doubles as machine-learning training
data. It is a working font today and an experiment in how typefaces might
evolve through machine learning tomorrow.
</p>
<p>
Point placement defaults to an 8-unit structural grid, with optical
refinements on a 2-unit subgrid, all inside a 1024-unit em. This discipline
lets a small open-weight language model (Virtua-12M) learn the design system
and generate new letterforms and weights that snap cleanly to the grid.
</p>
<p>
Designed by Eli Heuer, with tooling from the open-source Runebender font
editor. Virtua Grotesk is free and open source under the
<a href="https://openfontlicense.org">SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1</a>.
</p>
